WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.868 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hello!

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:06.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hi, guys. Um,
have you seen any movies?

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.709 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.212 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Any movies?

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
Any of them?
Have you guys seen any movies?

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah!
-Yeah? Which ones?

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Aquaman."
-"Aquaman."

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay. Okay.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm looking for
a specific movie.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.759 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:26.793 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-"Bohemian Rhapsody."

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:30.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm, I'm looking for
"Mama Mia" two.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.432 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Has anyone seen it?

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh! Good!

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.802 line:92%
I'm so -- The women, good.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.238
It's a wonderful film. I'll get
to the jokes in a second.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:41.341
I just want to make sure
everybody sees this movie.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a great film.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you don't know the premise,
basically

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:47.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
they take all the ABBA songs
that didn't quite fit into
"Mama Mia" one,

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.783 size:81% position:41%
and they sweep them up
into a little dustpan

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:52.786 size:78% position:39%
and blow them [blows]
onto a Greek island,

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:56.456
and they really make Greece
look like it's doing all right.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's wonderful.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.660 line:92%
Cher is in it. She's so good.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, how great is Cher,
you know?

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.197 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She's so great.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.633
She's in a lot of group scenes,
but they're all single shots,

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:10.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it's possible they let her
shoot it from home.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.573
Yeah. I guess I should say
kind of close to the top,

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.708 line:92%
I do have a very specific voice.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:18.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of people say it sounds
like I'm about to cry.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:22.348
But I just want to let you know,
I'm not about to cry.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.851 line:92%
I'm actually about to laugh.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:27.487 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.689 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:32.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's nice you guys
are all out here.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.028 line:92%
Are you guys night people?

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:37.630 size:81% position:41%
[ Audience cheering ]
Got some night people.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can always tell
the night people

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.601
'cause they're like,
"What are we doing after this?"

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.570 line:92%
It's like, can you imagine?

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sounds so terrible --
the reward for going here

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.109 size:81% position:41% line:92%
is you get to go home.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought I was maybe
a morning person

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause of how much
I hate the night,

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.447 size:78% position:39% line:92%
but then I got a job,

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it turns out
I'm not supposed to wake up.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was kind of bummed,
'cause I was like,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Maybe I don't have a time,"
you know?

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.391 line:92%
But I recently found my time.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:09.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am the "hour before lunch"
person.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.930 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.466 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Yeah, thank you. Thanks.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.735 line:92%
Maybe you guys are, as well.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. That's when
I'm really excited,

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.006 line:92%
I'm really curious, you know,

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.242 line:92%
because lunch can be anything.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.210 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You know? Like, Tariq,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
can I ask you what you had
for lunch today?

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.948 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Onions.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:32.385 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-What is that? What?

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Onions -- it's a --
I guess it's a vegetable.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.893 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Lunch can be anything.

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get so excited
about the possibilities,

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you know I'm always
gonna get soup.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.734 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.269 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And soup sucks.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:53.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's either too hot
or it's just wet.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:54.207 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.342
You take the first bite of soup,
you better like it

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause that's all the rest
of the bites.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
If you get a different bite,

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
something's messed up
with the soup.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:05.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
That joke was for
the soup haters.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
This next one's
much more universal.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.856
Here we go.
You know this situation,
you know what I'm talking about.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.991
You know what I'm saying,
you know what I'm talking about.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know -- you --
You're at home.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.029
Everybody knows it.
You know what I'm talking about?

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're at home.
You know what I mean?

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.399
And you're sitting down.
You know what I'm talking about?

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:21.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you're sitting down
and you're at home?
You know what I mean?

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:24.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're opening
your Russian nesting dolls?

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.371 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know what I mean?

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're getting
smaller and smaller?

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.141 line:92%
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you ever get to
the tinniest one

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:32.345 size:84% position:42%
and you think, "Hey,
this should be edible"?

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.047 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.215
Just a little crunchy something,
no big deal.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:38.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
You go to your friend's house,
you're like, "Did you
eat yours?"

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.086 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Yes. You?"

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.688 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Yeah, yeah."

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:45.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a problem
with online shopping.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I worry that
my online shopping habits

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:51.998
will, like, kind of start going
into real-store behavior,

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:56.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
like I'll just start breaking
into stores at 1:00 A.M.,

00:03:56.069 --> 00:04:00.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
putting nine things in a cart,
and leaving.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.408 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I really like
online shopping

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause the reviews, I think
they're really helpful,

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're also
pretty indicative

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.950 line:92%
of the political climate.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:11.384 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:14.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I was on the L.L. Bean
website recently,

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:18.524
and you know L.L. Bean is where
coats go to church.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:23.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was reading
this scathing review

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.565 line:92%
this woman left about a coat.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:27.300 line:92%
It was horrible. She was like,

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.869 line:92%
"The wind sneaks up the back.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.038 size:84% position:42% line:92%
The zipper never works.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:34.307 line:92%
And the material is loud.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:34.941 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
One star."

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:38.811
And I can't help but wonder if
she had written the same review

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.546 line:92%
when Obama was President.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.315 line:92%
It would have just been like,

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:45.485
"Coat's not great, but it gives
me hope for a better coat."

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:49.922
All right, that's my time.
Thank you very much. Thank you.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.958 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.593 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That is...

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:55.762 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah!

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:58.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
...Jo Firestone!

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:03.770 line:92%
For more, go to jofirestone.com.

